label ceiling
sensol: Dıp ʎon ɥǝɐɹ? Sowat's ıs ƪoınınƃ ɐ clawqoʇ's nǝʇʍoɹʞ!
kintan: ⊥ɥǝʎ'ɹǝ ʇoo pıɟɟǝɹǝnʇ! Mɥɐʇ ıɟ ʇɥǝʎ pon'ʇ 1ǝʇ ıʇ nsǝ ıʇs ɯɐƃnǝʇs ɐnʎɯoɹǝ?
[end_timeline]
label Patch
if {patch} == true:
	Ignore Patch.
else:
	patch: Hey Green. Catch!
	Patch throws something at your face.
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label Patch_response
if {response} == "right":
	You dodge the thing.
	green: I'm not doing that.
elif {response} == "neutral":
	You slapped whatever that was back at Patch.
	patch: HEY! The least you could do is catch it.
	green: And give you the satisfaction? That was plastic!
else:
	You activate your magnets too late. It dinged off your head.
	patch: Nothing to say?
	It's a good thing robots can't cry.
set {patch} = true
[end_timeline]
label group_b
if {group_b} == true:
	kintan: group b final words
else:
	Sheen: What if we make something fun like a claw machine?
	Rote: We are claw bots. We barely have the mobility for joy sticks.
	screen: But imagine! Claws squared!
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label group_b_response
if {response} == "right":
	green: That's such a cool idea!
	Sheen: See! Green agrees with me!
	Rote: Ugh. Don't enable it, Green.
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: What if you just attach another longer claw to yourself?
	screen: Oh hey Green. Don't have materials for that but we'll keep cooking.
else:
	green: What are you talking about?
	Rote: You wouldn't get it.
set {group_b} = true
[end_timeline]
label group_a
if {group_a} == true:
	...
else:
	beam: ...so smug! You should've seen how Green shrugged me off.
	beam: I need Haptor to stop comparing us, like I need to be reminded...
	[signal arg="beam leaves"]
	beam: ...Talk to you later. I gotta go to my shift.
	[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label group_a_response
if {response} == "right":
	green: Is Beam okay?
	vale: Just work problems. Don't worry about it.
	gnuna: Just let Beam know that we'll be by for the shift change.
	green: Okay.
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: Hey guys. How's everything?
	vale: It's okay. We'll be by later for the shift change.
	gnuna: See you later!
else:
	green: What are we talking about?
	vale: It's nothing you should worry about.
	green: Oh okay.
set {group_a} = true
[end_timeline]
label Terminal
It's a little old and laggy, but we don't really have the parts to repair it. We do so much recycling though. If only we could have some of those pieces.
[end_timeline]
label Elevator
I don’t have the credentials to use it. Cable probably does.
[end_timeline]
label Locked Door
It’s rusting at the edges, which is weird because there’s no oxygen here anymore.
[end_timeline]
label Trak
[signal arg="respond"]
[end_timeline]
label Trak_response
if {response} == "right":
	green: How can I help?
	trak: I'm okay. You don't have to stay here.
	green: Nope, I'm sitting here.
	trak: Oh okay.
elif {response} == "neutral":
	green: ...
	trak: ...
	green: Let's get you home.
else:
	green: I can realign whatever's inside with my magnets.
	trak: You know your magnets aren't good enough for that.
	green: Ouch. Worth a try.
trak: ...
trak: You've been talking less than when you first started here.
green: Let's not talk about that. It feels like calling for rand() on a good day
trak: How else would I find quality entertainment?
trak: Big hits such as\: Why do your arms have smaller arms?
green: I didn't even realize there was a difference to begin with until Patch pointed at my magnets and told me to climb a wall.
[signal arg="trak_restore"]
trak: Not like anyone could except for the really old magnet bots.
green: I need a software reprogramming. For better communication analysis or something.
trak: I'm not sure if that's even possible. I just need a hardware upgrade if anything.
trak: At least it wasn't the insane rush like when the humans were still around. One of my network mates were functioning then and it said its humans were really bad at maintaining their bots.
trak: At least we got each other right? Basement solidarity!
green: That sounds so bad!
green: But yeah. We got something.
[signal arg="final"]
[end_timeline]